{"archetypes":[{"name":"resume-state","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Large python ship/run_logs changes add persisted resume state, counters, and hydration paths that need state-machine scrutiny.","prompt_body":"Investigate how persisted ship state is read, validated, preserved, and rewritten across fresh runs, blocked resumes, terminal outcomes, and re-entry paths. Look for stale or corrupt state causing incorrect phase selection, lost counters, unsafe fallback to fresh work, or incorrect run-log status decisions. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"pr-identity","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds GitHub PR identity, branch, repo, merge, and fork handling that can fail at integration boundaries.","prompt_body":"Examine the PR identity and GitHub integration paths, including repo slug checks, branch/head validation, PR URL parsing, merged or closed PR handling, forked-target modes, and skipped-merge signal thresholds. Focus on cases where local git state, persisted state, and GitHub responses disagree or are unavailable. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"ci-loop","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"CI monitor outcome handling and retry counters interact with resume state and iteration budgets.","prompt_body":"Review the CI monitor and ship-loop changes for correct handling of local-unfixable, transient bailouts, fix-only reruns, merge retries, rebase retries, and iteration caps. Check whether counters are incremented, persisted, or intentionally not consumed in every monitor outcome path. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"git-restore","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"The design pause loader now restores committed blobs manually and changes marker deletion semantics around untrusted issue data.","prompt_body":"Inspect the design pause restore path that enumerates snapshots with git ls-tree and materializes files with git show. Pay close attention to path containment, NUL-delimited iteration, temp-file cleanup, structured failure tokens, marker retention on failure, and marker deletion after successful install. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"contract-drift","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The staged plan centers on design pause changes, while the diff also includes substantial Python ship workflow changes and contract docs.","prompt_body":"Compare the implementation surface against the stated plan and the repository contracts touched by docs, shell scripts, Python modules, and regression tests. Look for undocumented behavior changes, mismatched contracts between .md files and scripts, or unrelated workflow changes that should have their own plan authority. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
